(   [Problem Statement]: Differentiate systematically between 'Low-Fidelity' and 'High-Fidelity' prototypes across the five dimensions of fidelity formulated by McCurdy et al. \(Visual, Breadth, Depth, Interactivity, Data Model\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Five Dimensions of Prototype Fidelity \(McCurdy et al.\):) Tj
T*
(   - Dimension 1: Visual Refinement: The degree to which the prototype's visual styling resembles) Tj
T*
(   the finished product \(fonts, colors, whitespace, margins, iconography\).) Tj
T*
(   - Dimension 2: Breadth of Functionality: The range and diversity of different features and) Tj
T*
(   screens represented across the horizontal surface of the application.) Tj
T*
(   - Dimension 3: Depth of Functionality: How deeply an individual specific task can be executed) Tj
T*
(   end-to-end through real or simulated logic.) Tj
T*
(   - Dimension 4: Richness of Interactivity: The responsiveness of the UI to human inputs) Tj
T*
(   \(micro-animations, transition easing, drag-and-drop, gesture support\).) Tj
T*
(   - Dimension 5: Richness of Data Model: Whether the prototype operates on static hardcoded mock) Tj
T*
(   strings or dynamic, realistic, domain-specific data with realistic edge lengths.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Comparative Matrix:) Tj
T*
(   - Low-Fidelity \(Lo-Fi\) Prototypes \(Paper Sketches, Cardboard, Rough Wireframes\):) Tj
T*
(   * Visual: Minimal \(grayscale, hand-drawn lines, generic fonts\).) Tj
T*
(   * Breadth: Narrow or wide, but purely static facades.) Tj
T*
(   * Depth: Extremely shallow; operations are simulated manually by a human facilitator.) Tj
T*
(   * Interactivity: Manual paper swapping, no digital transitions.) Tj
T*
(   * Data Model: Static placeholder text, simulated inputs.) Tj
T*
(   - High-Fidelity \(Hi-Fi\) Prototypes \(Interactive Figma, Clickable React/Flutter Mockups\):) Tj
T*
(   * Visual: Pixel-perfect, 100% brand-compliant design tokens and typography.) Tj
T*
ET

