(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the step-by-step methodology of conducting a 'Paper Prototyping' usability test. Define the distinct operational responsibilities of the Facilitator, the Human Computer, and the Observers.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Preparation of Physical Artifacts:) Tj
T*
(   - Draw mobile or desktop interface screens on heavy cardstock \(base screens\).) Tj
T*
(   - Create separate paper cutout overlays for dropdown menus, modal alerts, keyboard trays, and) Tj
T*
(   loading spinners.) Tj
T*
(   - Use removable adhesive tape or clear acetate sheets for dynamic user writing.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Role Division and Strict Operational Protocols:) Tj
T*
(   - Role 1: The Facilitator:) Tj
T*
(   * Interacts directly with the participant. Explains the purpose: 'We are testing the paper) Tj
T*
(   sketches, not you.') Tj
T*
(   * Hands task scenarios to the user. Encourages the Think-Aloud protocol: 'Tell me what you are) Tj
T*
(   looking at and what you expect to happen.') Tj
T*
(   * Intervenes if the participant gets hopelessly stuck, keeping the session moving without) Tj
T*
(   hinting at solutions.) Tj
T*
(   - Role 2: The 'Human Computer':) Tj
T*
(   * Strictly SILENT throughout the entire session. Must never speak, apologize, or explain) Tj
T*
(   buttons!) Tj
T*
(   * Sits beside the paper mockup with organized stacks of paper screens and overlays.) Tj
T*
(   * Translates user finger taps into physical state updates: when the user taps 'Settings', the) Tj
T*
