(   * MDPI \(1x baseline - Android\) / Non-Retina \(1x - Web\).) Tj
T*
(   * XHDPI \(2x - Apple @2x Retina, Android XHDPI\).) Tj
T*
(   * XXHDPI \(3x - Apple @3x iPhone Pro, Android XXHDPI\).) Tj
T*
(   * Scale Factors of 1.5x \(HDPI - older Android displays\).) Tj
T*
(   - Mathematical Cleanliness:) Tj
T*
(   * If an engineer uses an odd number \(e.g., 7px or 13px padding\):) Tj
T*
(   - At 1.5x scaling: 7 * 1.5 = 10.5 physical pixels!) Tj
T*
(   - The graphics GPU cannot render half-pixels; it must interpolate, rendering blurry,) Tj
T*
(   anti-aliased, smeared edges.) Tj
T*
(   * Because 8 is cleanly divisible by 2 and 4, multiplying 8 by ANY standard scaling factor \(1x,) Tj
T*
(   1.5x, 2x, 3x, 4x\) ALWAYS yields a perfect whole integer:) Tj
T*
(   - 8 * 1.0 = 8px.) Tj
T*
(   - 8 * 1.5 = 12px.) Tj
T*
(   - 8 * 2.0 = 16px.) Tj
T*
(   - 8 * 3.0 = 24px.) Tj
T*
(   - 8 * 4.0 = 32px.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Engineering Efficiency:) Tj
T*
(   - Eliminates endless designer-developer debates over arbitrary 1px and 3px spacing nudges,) Tj
T*
(   standardizing layout tokens across the engineering pipeline.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
