/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze Nick Swinmurn's founding of Zappos as an exemplar of the 'Wizard of Oz MVP'. Contrast this approach with the catastrophic over-engineering of Webvan during the Dot-Com era.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Zappos and the Lean Wizard of Oz MVP \(1999\):) Tj
T*
(   - Hypothesis: Customers have the desire and willingness to purchase shoes online without) Tj
T*
(   physically trying them on first.) Tj
T*
(   - Lean Validation: Nick Swinmurn did not raise $50 million, build automated warehouses, or sign) Tj
T*
(   complex inventory contracts.) Tj
T*
(   - The Execution: He walked to local shoe stores in San Francisco, photographed shoes on) Tj
T*
(   display, and posted images on a barebones website \(Shoesite.com\). When a customer clicked) Tj
T*
(   'Buy', he walked to the store, purchased the shoes at retail price, and mailed them from the) Tj
T*
(   post office.) Tj
T*
(   - Result: Validated the core value hypothesis with near-zero capital investment before raising) Tj
T*
(   venture capital to engineer supply chains.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Webvan and the Dot-Com Over-Engineering Catastrophe \(1999-2001\):) Tj
T*
(   - Hypothesis: Consumers want online grocery home delivery.) Tj
T*
(   - Brute-Force Over-Engineering: Instead of testing whether consumers wanted online groceries,) Tj
T*
(   Webvan raised $800 million and immediately built massive, automated $30-million robotic) Tj
T*
(   warehouses with miles of conveyor belts in 26 cities before securing customer demand.) Tj
T*
(   - Catastrophic Collapse: Customer order volume was a tiny fraction of projected capacity.) Tj
T*
(   Massive fixed capital depreciation and warehouse overhead forced Webvan into Chapter 11) Tj
T*
(   bankruptcy in under 24 months, burning $1.2 billion.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Strategic Lesson:) Tj
T*
(   - Validate customer behavior manually with a Wizard of Oz MVP before engineering) Tj
T*
(   multi-million-dollar infrastructure.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 9:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
