(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the role of 'User Flows' in bridging digital wireframes with backend systems architecture. Construct a detailed user flow diagram for a user resetting a forgotten password.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Architectural Role of User Flows:) Tj
T*
(   - While wireframes illustrate isolated screens, User Flows map the temporal and logical) Tj
T*
(   journeys connecting user intentions, frontend interactive states, backend API transactions, and) Tj
T*
(   system decision branches.) Tj
T*
(   - They prevent architectural blind spots by explicitly modeling error states, timeouts, and) Tj
T*
(   asynchronous external events \(e.g., email delivery\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. User Flow Construction: Password Reset Workflow:) Tj
T*
(   - [Start: User on Login Screen]) Tj
T*
(   |) Tj
T*
(   v) Tj
T*
(   [User taps 'Forgot Password?']) Tj
T*
(   |) Tj
T*
(   v) Tj
T*
(   [Screen: Enter Registered Email Address]) Tj
T*
(   |) Tj
T*
