(   - Mobile-First mandates designing for the smallest screen \(375x667px\) first, followed by) Tj
T*
(   progressive enhancement as screen real estate expands to tablets and desktops.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Enforcing Ruthless Prioritization:) Tj
T*
(   - A 375px mobile viewport has approximately 80% less visible screen real estate than a standard) Tj
T*
(   desktop browser above the fold.) Tj
T*
(   - This physical constraint eliminates superficial fluff. Product teams cannot afford to clutter) Tj
T*
(   the screen with secondary navigation bars, marketing banners, and tertiary widgets.) Tj
T*
(   - The team is forced to identify the single most critical 'Job-To-Be-Done' for that screen,) Tj
T*
(   placing the primary action front and center.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Progressive Enhancement Across Breakpoints:) Tj
T*
(   - Mobile \(375px\): Linear single-column layout, bottom navigation bar, collapsed hamburger) Tj
T*
(   menus, thumb-friendly 48px touch targets.) Tj
T*
(   - Tablet \(768px\): Two-column layout, sidebar navigation, expanding summary cards.) Tj
T*
(   - Desktop \(1200px+\): Multi-column layouts, contextual hover inspector panes, advanced data) Tj
T*
(   grids with fixed table headers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
