/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 18:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the 'Concierge vs. Wizard of Oz' MVP trade-off. In what specific circumstances is a Concierge MVP vastly superior to a Wizard of Oz facade?) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Definitional Contrast:) Tj
T*
(   - Wizard of Oz \(WOz\): The front-end appears fully automated; the user thinks an algorithm is) Tj
T*
(   executing their request, while a human works secretly behind the scenes.) Tj
T*
(   - Concierge: The human service is fully transparent; the user knowingly interacts with a human) Tj
T*
(   consultant/operator who delivers the value proposition by hand.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. When Concierge is Vastly Superior:) Tj
T*
(   - Circumstance 1: High Domain Complexity & Uncharted Problem Spaces:) Tj
T*
(   * When the engineering team has zero idea how to write the underlying algorithm because the) Tj
T*
(   rules of the domain are completely unknown \(e.g., custom enterprise tax structuring\). A human) Tj
T*
(   concierge converses with the client, extracting domain heuristics that can later be codified) Tj
T*
(   into algorithms.) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
