T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Asynchronous Distributed Systems Reality:) Tj
T*
(   - In financial mobile transactions, network connections are inherently unreliable \(e.g., user) Tj
T*
(   walking into an elevator while tapping 'Pay $100'\).) Tj
T*
(   - Designing wireframes that model only the instant 'Payment Successful' screen creates) Tj
T*
(   catastrophic production vulnerabilities.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. The Distributed Network Timeout Edge Case:) Tj
T*
(   - Scenario: The client sends a payment HTTP request; the server processes the charge and debits) Tj
T*
(   the bank account, but the mobile cellular connection drops before the 'HTTP 200 OK' response) Tj
T*
(   reaches the smartphone!) Tj
T*
(   - The UX Failure: The app displays: 'Connection Failed - Payment Error'.) Tj
T*
(   - The Human Panic: The user immediately taps 'Pay $100' again! The user is double-charged $200,) Tj
T*
(   balance plummets, and furious customer calls swamp the support center.) Tj
T*
