(   [Problem Statement]: Evaluate the 'PalmPilot Wooden Block Prototype' designed by Jeff Hawkins. How did carry-along physical ergonomics de-risk handheld digital computing before silicon manufacturing?) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Historical Context of Handheld Computing \(1995\):) Tj
T*
(   - Apple's Newton MessagePad had recently collapsed in the market due to its bulky size, heavy) Tj
T*
(   weight, and fragile battery life.) Tj
T*
(   - Industry experts claimed handheld personal digital assistants \(PDAs\) were a failed product) Tj
T*
(   category.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Jeff Hawkins's Radical Low-Fidelity Prototype:) Tj
T*
(   - Hawkins believed the Newton failed because it did not fit naturally into a person's shirt) Tj
T*
(   pocket.) Tj
T*
(   - He went to his home garage, carved a block of wood to the exact dimensions of a shirt pocket,) Tj
T*
(   and glued a paper printout of an interface onto the surface.) Tj
T*
(   - He carved a small wooden chopstick to simulate the physical stylus pen.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. The Longitudinal Immersion Experiment:) Tj
T*
(   - Hawkins carried the wooden block in his shirt pocket for several months everywhere he went.) Tj
T*
(   - During business meetings, when someone asked to schedule lunch, he pulled out the wooden) Tj
T*
(   block, tapped the paper calendar with his wooden stylus, and observed whether the physical) Tj
T*
(   interaction felt natural or socially awkward.) Tj
T*
(   - When checking addresses, he took out the block to test one-handed reachability.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Engineering Impact:) Tj
T*
(   - Proved that the physical form factor and immediate pocket accessibility were the foundational) Tj
T*
(   value drivers, guiding Palm to engineer hardware that fit those exact wooden dimensions,) Tj
T*
(   creating the fastest-selling consumer electronics product in history.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
